  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(5, 30, 60)\n\n(11, 66, 132)\n\n**Logic:** Third no. = [{(First no.) × 6} + (Second no.)]\n\n**(5, 30, 60) →**\n\n⇒ [(5 × 6) + 30]\n\n⇒ (30 + 30) = 60\n\n**(11, 66, 132) →**\n\n⇒ [(11 × 6) + 66]\n\n⇒ (66 + 66) = 132\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. **(6, 42, 148) →\n\n⇒ [(6 × 6) + 42]\n\n⇒ (36 + 42) = 78\n\n**2. (14, 84, 168) →**\n\n⇒ [(14 × 6) + 84]\n\n⇒ (84 + 84) = **168**\n\n**3. **(14, 16, 118) →\n\n⇒ [(14 × 6) + 16]\n\n⇒ (84 + 16) = 100\n\n**4.** (2, 10, 16) →\n\n⇒ [(2 × 6) + 10]\n\n⇒ (12 + 10) = 22\n\nHere, (14, 84, 168) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
